<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-3">3 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Northern Ireland comes into being</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Government of Ireland Act took effect, partitioning Ireland and creating Northern Ireland from six north-eastern counties with its own parliament. Partition remains in place today.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-11">11 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier is dedicated at Arlington</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">President Harding presided as an unidentified American soldier from the Western Front was buried at Arlington National Cemetery. A year earlier, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> had interred their own unknown warriors.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-6">6 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Anglo-Irish Treaty is signed</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Irish and British delegates signed a treaty in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> creating the Irish Free State as a dominion, with Northern Ireland able to opt out. Divisions over it led to the Irish Civil War.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/kronstadt-rebellion" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kronstadt-rebellion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/kronstadt-rebellion">Kronstadt rebellion</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Kronstadt rebellion was a revolt in March 1921 by sailors, soldiers and workers of the naval fortress of Kronstadt near Petrograd against the Bolshevik government.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-riga">Peace of Riga</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Peace of Riga was signed on 18 March 1921 between Poland on one side and Soviet Russia and Soviet Ukraine on the other, ending the Polish–Soviet War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sakarya" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-sakarya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sakarya">Battle of Sakarya</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Sakarya was fought from 23 August to 13 September 1921 along the Sakarya River west of Ankara, during the Greco-Turkish War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ankara-1921">Treaty of Ankara (1921)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Ankara (1921) was the agreement signed on 20 October 1921 between France and the Turkish nationalist government of the Grand National Assembly, negotiated by Henry Franklin-Bouillon.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/coto-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/coto-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/coto-war">Coto War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Coto War was a brief border conflict between Panama and Costa Rica in February and March 1921 over the Coto region on the Pacific side of their disputed frontier.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/russo-persian-treaty-of-friendship-1921" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russo-persian-treaty-of-friendship-1921.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/russo-persian-treaty-of-friendship-1921">Russo-Persian Treaty of Friendship (1921)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Russo-Persian Treaty of Friendship was signed in Moscow on 26 February 1921 between Soviet Russia and Persia.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/pact-of-union-1921">Pact of Union (1921)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Pact of Union was an agreement signed at San José, Costa Rica, in January 1921, on the centenary of Central American independence, to recreate a federal union of the isthmus.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/venice-protocol">Venice Protocol</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Venice Protocol was an agreement signed on 13 October 1921 between Austria and Hungary under Italian mediation to settle the dispute over Burgenland.</p></div></li></ol></section>
